QUESTION 2: EMPLOYEE PERFORMANCE EVALUATION
============================================================

A company wants to evaluate the performance of its employees. Each employee has an employee ID, employee name, salary, and three performance scores. The three scores represent:
1. Technical skill
2. Communication skill
3. Teamwork

The performance scores should not be stored in a fixed normal array. Instead, memory for the three scores should be allocated dynamically using a pointer when an employee object is created.

The program should provide functions to accept employee details, accept the three performance scores, calculate the average performance score, increase the employee salary by a specified percentage, and display complete employee information.

A separate function outside the class should receive an employee object by reference and evaluate its performance. If the employee's average score satisfies the required performance condition, the employee should receive a 10% salary increment. Otherwise, the salary should remain unchanged.

The program should also demonstrate proper resource management by releasing the dynamically allocated memory using a destructor when the employee object is destroyed.

The main program should be menu driven with operations such as:
1. Enter employee details
2. Enter performance scores
3. Calculate and display average score
4. Evaluate employee and update salary if eligible
5. Display employee details
6. Exit

The menu should repeat until the user selects exit.


