QUESTION 4: GCD, LCM AND COMMON FACTORS OF TWO NUMBERS
============================================================

Design a C++ program to perform mathematical operations on two positive integers.

Create a class that stores two integer values.

The program should calculate the Greatest Common Divisor using the Euclidean Algorithm.

Example:
48 and 18
48 % 18 = 12
18 % 12 = 6
12 % 6 = 0
GCD = 6

The program should not calculate the GCD by simply checking every possible divisor.

Using the calculated GCD, determine the Least Common Multiple using:
LCM = (Number1 × Number2) / GCD

The program should also identify and display all common factors of the two numbers.

It should determine whether the two numbers are relatively prime. Two numbers are relatively prime when their GCD is equal to 1.

The user should be allowed to enter a new pair of numbers without restarting the application.

Expected Menu:

===== NUMBER OPERATIONS MENU =====
1. Enter Two Numbers
2. Calculate GCD
3. Calculate LCM
4. Display Common Factors
5. Check Whether Numbers are Relatively Prime
6. Enter New Numbers
7. Exit

The program should terminate only when option 7 is selected.


